    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0101" n="9" xml:id="pg9"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Marshal Stalin</hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d9-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hyde
                                Park</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-18"
                            >June 18, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">To: Marshal Stalin</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">From: The President</p>
                <p>I am a few days late in answering your message as I was away when it came.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d9-f2"/> I fully subscribe to what Mr. Churchill telegraphed
                    you and I want to assure you that at this time we are really doing everything
                    that is possible. I hope you will understand that the shipping situation is
                    still tight, though we have been greatly encouraged by the better progress of
                    our anti-submarine campaign during the last two months which shows us a good net
                    gain in available ships.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d9-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d9-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the White House, and forwarded by the White House Map Room, in paraphrase
                    (marked “Secret” and “Operational Priority”), to the United States Naval
                    Attaché, Moscow, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d9-f2" n="2" xml:id="d9-f2-content">
                <p>Roosevelt was at Charlottesville, Virginia, June 11–13, 1943.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
